		{"id":"e86028b7ec7c0987","type":"text","text":"[[Belmont City.canvas]]\n#RavenLoft ","x":-780,"y":-400,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"75c8a44e53d74187","type":"text","text":"The Copper Cask & Clockwork\nNestled in the bustling, steam-vented industrial district of your city, The Copper Cask & Clockwork stands as a testament to the marriage of traditional alchemy and modern mechanical engineering.\nThe building itself is a former watchmaking factory, repurposed with massive brass conduits and intricate piping that hums with the rhythm of the brewing process.\nThe Proprietor: Elara \"Gear-Tap\" Vance\nElara is a no-nonsense, sharp-witted artificer who views brewing as the ultimate mechanical puzzle. She sports brass-rimmed magnifying goggles, a leather apron scorched by steam, and a mechanical prosthetic arm she built herself to handle heavy boiling vats.\n\t• Personality: Pragmatic, obsessively precise, and fiercely protective of her equipment.\n\t• Motivation: She is currently obsessed with perfecting the \"Pressure-Fermentation\" method, which aims to create the crispest, fastest-carbonated spirits in the realm.\nSignature Offerings\nThe brewery is famous for its Automated Tap-Wall, where patrons pull brass levers to dispense drinks directly from cooled copper coils.\nDrink Name\tDescription\tEffect (Flavor)\nPiston-Punched Porter\tA thick, dark ale filtered through pulverized obsidian.\tNotes of burnt espresso and cold iron.\nClockwork Cider\tFermented with alchemical catalysts to ensure 100% consistency.\tExceptionally tart with a lingering effervescent kick.\nHigh-Pressure Hops\tAn IPA brewed inside a sealed steam-tank to lock in aromatic oils.\tFloral, sharp, and leaves the tongue slightly numb.\nSteam-Engine Stout\tBoiled over controlled elemental fire.\tSmoky, heavy, and served at exactly 45°C.\nNotable Features\n\t• The Atmospheric Chiller: A massive brass orb in the center of the bar that cycles icy runoff water through the building, keeping the taproom refreshingly cool despite the boiler room next door.\n\t• The \"Hiccup\" Engine: A small, erratic steam engine mounted above the bar that whistles a rhythmic, melancholic tune whenever a new batch is ready to be tapped.\n\t• The Maintenance Crew: Elara employs several small, clanking mechanical spiders (Clockwork Scuttlers) that scurry across the rafters to tighten loose steam valves and clean spills before they hit the floor.\n\tNote: The brewery maintains a strict \"no magic\" rule for brewing—Elara insists that her mechanical precision is far superior to any wizard’s clumsy spellwork.","x":-780,"y":-240,"width":1285,"height":620},
		{"id":"119c501326808d0e","type":"text","text":"Unhileg Arcanum\n\nVenthra's shop\n\nHorn of Silent Alarm - 250gp\n\nPotion of Growth - 400gp\n\nRing of Invisibility - 15000gp\n","x":640,"y":-200,"width":440,"height":270},
